<title>TAIWAN: Central Insurance limit up in debut.</title>
<headline>Central Insurance limit up in debut.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Central Insurance went limit up on its listing debut in late trade on Wednesday, with brokers expecting its &quot;honeymoon run&quot; to last two more sessions.</p>
<p>With 20 minutes left, Central Insurance had soared by the seven-percent daily limit or T$3 to T$51.</p>
<p>Only 2,000 shares were traded.  </p>
<p>Central Insurance, a state-run general insurance firm, is Taiwan's fourth largest insurance company with total net assets of T$1.08 billion.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the typical honeymoon period jump, and since it is considered a good firm the jump will probably extend for two more sessions,&quot; said George Hou of Jardine Fleming.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
